From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 04:33:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] updater: retry and resume the update download

The update screen downloaded a GitHub release asset with one call on the
shared client (30s read, 2min call). From mainland China the first
connection to release-assets.githubusercontent.com often stalls or is
reset after the handshake. OkHttp does not retry that read inside one
call, so the exception deleted update.apk and the button became Retry.
The next tap was a new call and usually succeeded.

This download uses its own client (60s read, 10min call), at most 4
attempts, and delays of 2/4/8 seconds. IOException and HTTP 5xx are
retried; 416 deletes the file and starts from zero; other 4xx fail
immediately. A 206 response is appended and a 200 response is rewritten.
The partial file is kept until the final failure. Starting again drops
update.apk only when packageManager can read a versionCode from it.
Failure shows timeout, a dropped connection, the HTTP code, or a storage
write error instead of the exception text.

Anikku already resumes through upstream NetworkHelper.downloadFileWithResume
(5 attempts), so this is not ported there. Animeko uses a different
downloader and switches to the universal package after a failure.
